From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] misc: decd: declare the single-mapping DMA constraint

DECD has no scatter-gather. It is programmed with one base address and a
stride, and derives the chroma address arithmetically, so an import has to
resolve to a single mapping spanning the whole buffer or patch 0072 rejects it.

The driver never told the DMA core that. With no dma_parms set,
dma_get_max_seg_size() returns the 64 KiB default and the IOMMU layer stops
coalescing there, so whether an import collapsed to one segment came down to how
fragmented physical memory happened to be at the time. Measured on the bench,
the same binary on the same boot:

    run 1   1 segment, whole buffer, 0x05600070 = 0xFDC00000
    run 2   14 segment(s), first 20480 of 1384448 bytes -- rejected

With the constraint declared, five consecutive runs mapped as a single IOVA with
zero rejections, and throughput went from 27.16 to ~29.8 fps against a 29.97 fps
clip -- the unexplained ~1 s deficit over 300 frames was the fragmented mapping.

Note this makes the *mapping* deterministic; it does not by itself put video on
the panel. See docs/handoff-2026-08-31.md.

--- a/drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/decd_core.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/decd_core.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <linux/cdev.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
+#include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/fs.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
@@ -122,6 +123,22 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(dec->rst_bus_disp))
 		return PTR_ERR(dec->rst_bus_disp);
 
+	/*
+	 * DECD has no scatter-gather: it is programmed with one base address
+	 * and a stride, and derives the chroma address arithmetically. An
+	 * import must therefore resolve to a single mapping spanning the whole
+	 * buffer.
+	 *
+	 * Without dma_parms the DMA core assumes the 64 KiB default maximum
+	 * segment size and stops coalescing there, so a physically scattered
+	 * buffer comes back as many segments even behind a working IOMMU --
+	 * measured on the bench as 14 segments with a 20480-byte first one,
+	 * against the same buffer that mapped as a single IOVA when memory
+	 * happened to be less fragmented. Say what the hardware actually needs
+	 * instead of depending on the allocator's luck.
+	 */
+	dma_set_max_seg_size(dev, UINT_MAX);
+
 	dec->fence_ctx = dec_fence_context_alloc("dec");
 	if (IS_ERR(dec->fence_ctx))
 		return PTR_ERR(dec->fence_ctx);
